{
  "notes": "Chiptune from a 1989 cabinet, G dorian, 128 BPM, two-bar game loops with a chord every two beats. Every synth is the LOFI chip voice: a pulse arpeggio (8BIT ARP with the chip's octave warble) that runs sixteenth-note broken chords, a triangle bass (GB BASS) bouncing in octaves, and the player's thin 12.5 % pulse lead on the Smart Keys (GAME LEAD on the stepped NES-style envelope, with vibrato), over the CHIP kit's square kick and noise snare. Scenes: A idles on i (insert coin); B runs i III VII IV; C climbs ii III IV and falls to VII with an Alberti arpeggio and four on the floor; D waits on IV and i (continue?). ENERGY opens the arpeggio: quarter notes alone, then kick and bass, then snare, noise hats and eighth-note arps, then every sixteenth, ratchets and fills. All material is original.",
